Opus decoder: codec PLC on by default, runtime per-call decoder complexity
(finding #15), self-verification log line.

- `audio_decoder_opus.cc`: `generate_plc_` (WebRTC's own jitter-buffer-side
  concealment, independent of libopus's internal deep PLC) switches from
  opt-in (`WebRTC-Audio-OpusGeneratePlc/Enabled/`) to on-by-default; the
  same trial stays as the emergency kill switch (`/Disabled/` now turns it
  off, matching P4b/P5's convention of keeping only the two upstream
  trials the plan allows - WebRTC-EnableDtlsPqc and
  WebRTC-Audio-OpusGeneratePlc - as emergency-off switches, no new trial of
  our own). Also emits one "Q-AUDION opus-dec" self-verification log line
  per process (not per decoder instance, since renegotiation can recreate
  one), reporting `deep_plc_compiled`/`osce_compiled` (read from P4a's
  QAUDION_OPUS_DEEP_PLC/QAUDION_OPUS_OSCE self-report defines, propagated
  through third_party/opus's own public_configs), `codec_plc`, and the
  decoder's actual libopus complexity.
- `opus_interface.{h,cc}` (finding #15 - the actual runtime API): a new
  file-local `ApplyQaudionDecoderComplexity()` reads
  `webrtc::qaudion::OpusDecoderComplexity()` (P8; -1 = use
  kQaudionDefaultDecoderComplexity = 7) and calls
  `opus_decoder_ctl(state->decoder, OPUS_SET_COMPLEXITY(...))`. Called from
  three places: `WebRtcOpus_DecoderCreate` and `WebRtcOpus_DecoderInit`
  (`OPUS_RESET_STATE` drops libopus's own complexity tracking back to its
  internal default, so it has to be re-applied right after), and - the
  actual "mid-call" case finding #15 asks for - right before the
  `opus_decode()` call in `DecodeNative()`, the single choke point every
  decode path in this file goes through (`WebRtcOpus_Decode`, `DecodePlc`
  via an empty payload, and `WebRtcOpus_DecodeFec`). New accessor
  `WebRtcOpus_DecoderComplexity()` (OPUS_GET_COMPLEXITY) backs the
  self-verification log above.

  "on the decoder thread, ... never concurrently": DecodeNative() is only
  ever called from the thread that owns a given `OpusDecInst` (WebRTC's
  NetEQ decode call path owns one decoder instance exclusively), so calling
  `ApplyQaudionDecoderComplexity()` unconditionally right before every
  opus_decode() - rather than caching a "last applied generation" the way
  P5 does for the encoder - is both simpler and already race-free: there is
  nothing else that could be issuing a concurrent opus_decoder_ctl() on the
  same `state->decoder`. I chose not to add a generation-cache field to
  OpusDecInst for this because I do not have that struct's real definition
  (opus_inst.h) to safely add a field to; calling the CTL unconditionally
  on every decode instead is a few branches and an atomic load per frame
  (at 60 ms framing, ~16.7/s), not something worth risking a blind struct
  edit for.

  "No RTC_CHECK reachable from input": `OpusDecoderComplexity()` only ever
  returns -1 or a value webrtc::qaudion::SetOpusDecoderComplexity() already
  validated into 0..10 (P8); `kQaudionDefaultDecoderComplexity` is a
  compile-time constant. opus_decoder_ctl(OPUS_SET_COMPLEXITY(...)) never
  RTC_CHECKs on its argument (it is a plain libopus CTL that would return
  OPUS_BAD_ARG for something out of range, which this code never passes it
  anyway) - grepped opus_interface.cc for RTC_CHECK, none of them are on
  this path.

Order: 6th in the series (m150/series), right after P8 and P4a (whose
QAUDION_OPUS_DEEP_PLC/QAUDION_OPUS_OSCE defines and dnn/ sources this
patch's log line and default-PLC behavior assume are compiled in) and
before P5.

Touches (dir "."): modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/opus_interface.h,
modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/opus_interface.cc,
modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus.cc.

Verified: `git apply --check` and a real apply are clean against the
pinned webrtc-sdk/webrtc @ ba469aa2093ba950066258ca0a59a6fbd1295582
checkout, on top of P1 + P2 + P3(partial - port.cc not in this partial
checkout, not mine) + P8 already applied, in series order. Every symbol
this patch calls (opus_decoder_ctl, OPUS_SET_COMPLEXITY, OPUS_GET_COMPLEXITY,
WebRtcOpus_DecoderCreate/Init, DecodeNative's exact structure,
generate_plc_'s exact constructor position) was read from that same pinned
checkout, not assumed; `opus_int32` (used in the new
WebRtcOpus_DecoderComplexity) is already used elsewhere in the same file
(DecodeNative's `static_cast<opus_int32>(encoded_bytes)`). Grepped the
resulting tree for RTC_LOG of key/secret/salt/password (none in the
touched files) and for new RTC_CHECK (none added).

Not verified: `clang -fsyntax-only` (see the M150 brief's note that the
local machine has no toolchain; setting up enough of the WebRTC header
graph - abseil, jni_zero, the rest of modules/audio_coding - on the
Helsinki VPS to syntax-check a single .cc file would need close to a full
gclient sync of the source tree, which is not "cheap" and risks its disk
budget, so I did not attempt it).

